{
  "id": "ss.char.egg",
  "name": "Egg",
  "description": "The youngest, and not finished hatching: half the shell is still on its head, worn as a cap with the crack it came out through running down it and the broken edge zigzagging over the brow, and one blond curl stands out of the top. Lids most of the way down, a pacifier where the mouth would be, the shortest legs of the eight under a round onesie that still shows the grub's segment lines. The feelers are stubs; it never grew those either, and the fiction is least kind to this one because they were never given a signal to lose. Its weapon is a toy: a pair of Soldier mandibles bound at the elbow, carried in the near hand and thrown so they come back. Same dead organ as the rest, worn as a brooch. Drawn facing +x; the game flips it.",
